29. Generation stage, para_500, TOP_K = 5, all 10 questions

Ran generate_answer.py. All 10 answers matched the known correct figures from the golden set, including the MAT rate question.

MAT question investigated specifically, since note 26 predicted the correct chunk, 0131, would not be retrieved, and it indeed was not among the 5 retrieved chunks. The correct answer still surfaced because chunk 0222 at rank 2 contains a second, independent restatement of the same fact, "MAT is proposed to be made as a final tax and the corresponding rate is reduced from 15% to 14%," located in the Annexure to Part B rather than the main speech body where chunk 0131 sits. The document states this fact twice, in two different sections with different wording, and para_500 chunking happened to keep the annexure version intact even though it broke the main body version.

Important caveat: this is a property of this specific document having redundant statements of the same fact, not a property of para_500 chunking being reliable for facts that appear only once. The underlying chunk boundary problem identified in note 26 is still real and would still cause a failure for a fact not restated elsewhere in the document. This should not be read as "the MAT gap is fixed," only as "this specific instance of it happened to have a safety net."

Other notable check, Q7, Electronics Components Manufacturing Scheme: the model correctly computed the increase amount, ₹17,081 crore, as the difference between the stated new outlay, ₹40,000 crore, and the original outlay, ₹22,919 crore, mentioned in context. This is a simple grounded computation from numbers present in the retrieved chunks, not an invented figure, consistent with faithfulness rather than hallucination.

Overall generation stage result: 10 out of 10 correct answers, all traceable to retrieved chunks, no hallucination observed.

