36. Decision: para_750 as the sandbox conclusion

para_750, text-embedding-3-small, is the strongest chunking and embedding combination found across this bounded experiment. It matches para_500's full 10 out of 10 generation result while closing the one confirmed retrieval gap para_500 had, and does so without needing a coincidental restatement elsewhere in the document. Reasoning for the win, grounded in the sequence of findings across this session: paragraph aware chunking outperformed fixed size chunking at every size tested, note 22 and note 24; text-embedding-3-small outperformed text-embedding-3-large on this document and this chunking method, note 24, a genuinely different result from an earlier session's finding on a different chunking method, note 24's clarification; and 750 characters gives paragraph aware chunking enough room to keep a full point and its immediately following point together, which is exactly the unit size several answers in this speech actually depend on, without inflating chunk count anywhere near as much as jumping to 1000 would.

This closes the bounded chunking and embedding experiment as originally scoped: 2 methods, now effectively 3 sizes tested given the justified exception for 750, 2 embedding models, tested against a fixed 10 question golden set, retrieval and generation checked separately throughout.

